From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 15:16:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/haswell: Hide the EHCI controllers with the native
 RAM init

With the native RAM init, early_usb_init() routes every USB 2.0 port to
the xHCI controller, at every boot and S3 resume. The two EHCI
controllers stay enabled with nothing but their rate matching hubs: the
OS runs two empty controllers, with their wake events on GPE 0x0d.

Disable both in mainboard_enable(), before enumeration, as the
ExpressCard and Thunderbolt root ports already are (the helper now takes
the PCI slot too): at every boot and resume, pch_enable() then puts them
in D3hot and sets their function disable bits. Not with mrc.bin, which
starts the ports on EHCI.

TEST=Built lenovo/w541 with mrc.bin and with the native RAM init.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/mainboard.c | 26 ++++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/mainboard.c b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/mainboard.c
index eaeb0c8982..d3db15d9bd 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/mainboard.c
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/mainboard.c
@@ -50,16 +50,16 @@ const char *smbios_chassis_serial_number(void)
 	return smbios_system_serial_number();
 }
 
-/* Before enumeration: the PCH code then hides and powers down the port */
-static void disable_root_port(unsigned int func, const char *what)
+/* Before enumeration: the PCH code then hides the device (and powers down a port) */
+static void disable_pch_device(unsigned int slot, unsigned int func, const char *what)
 {
-	struct device *rp = pcidev_on_root(0x1c, func);
+	struct device *dev = pcidev_on_root(slot, func);
 
-	if (!rp || !rp->enabled)
+	if (!dev || !dev->enabled)
 		return;
 
-	printk(BIOS_INFO, "%s: disabling %s\n", what, dev_path(rp));
-	rp->enabled = 0;
+	printk(BIOS_INFO, "%s: disabling %s\n", what, dev_path(dev));
+	dev->enabled = 0;
 }
 
 static void mainboard_enable(struct device *dev)
@@ -71,9 +71,19 @@ static void mainboard_enable(struct device *dev)
 	/* W541: ExpressCard/34 slot on root port 3, Thunderbolt controller on 5 */
 	if (CONFIG(BOARD_LENOVO_THINKPAD_W541)) {
 		if (!get_uint_option("expresscard", 1))
-			disable_root_port(2, "ExpressCard");
+			disable_pch_device(0x1c, 2, "ExpressCard");
 		if (!get_uint_option("thunderbolt", 1))
-			disable_root_port(4, "Thunderbolt");
+			disable_pch_device(0x1c, 4, "Thunderbolt");
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * The native RAM init routes every USB port to the xHCI controller, at
+	 * every boot and resume (early_usb_init()): the EHCI controllers keep
+	 * only their rate matching hubs. With mrc.bin the ports start on EHCI.
+	 */
+	if (CONFIG(USE_NATIVE_RAMINIT)) {
+		disable_pch_device(0x1a, 0, "USB on xHCI");
+		disable_pch_device(0x1d, 0, "USB on xHCI");
 	}
 }
 
